cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Rupsha, or any measurement out of its ledger, please cite it."
title: "Rupsha: an autonomy stack for ground rovers"
abstract: >-
  A ROS 2 control, mission and perception stack for an autonomous ground rover:
  reflexes on a Pixhawk running ArduRover, thinking on a Raspberry Pi, one
  manifest that generates every verb and message, and a measurement ledger in
  which every shipped number names what measured it. Built on the fundamentals
  of the Mongla AUV stack. Nothing in this stack has driven outdoors yet.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fh1m/rupsha_ws"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
keywords:
  - mobile robotics
  - ground rover
  - ROS 2
  - ArduPilot
  - autonomy
  - University Rover Challenge
